# Title tags and meta descriptions

Every public page must follow these rules in both English and Albanian.

- **Title tag**: 40–50 characters.
- **Meta description**: 120–150 characters.
- If the title starts with "Agon", the description must not start with "Agon".

Count characters exactly (with `node -e "console.log('...'.length)"`), never estimate.

## Where they live

Keep every copy in sync when adding or changing a page:

- `<title>`, `meta name="description"`, `og:title`, `og:description`, `twitter:title`, `twitter:description` in the page HTML
- `meta.*.title` / `meta.*.desc` in `js/i18n.js` (EN and SQ blocks)
- `description` entries in `js/data.js`
- Blog posts: `dyn.<slug>.pageTitle` / `dyn.<slug>.seoDesc` in `js/i18n.js` and the post HTML; the visible headline (`dyn.<slug>.title`) is not the title tag

Check all pages before finishing, including new project and blog pages.

## Examples

```text
❌ Malaj Design Case Study | Agon Mustafaj                 (39)
✅ Malaj Design Website Case Study | Agon Mustafaj         (47)

❌ Agon Mustafaj | SEO Expert...  +  "Agon Mustafaj is an SEO expert..."
✅ Agon Mustafaj | SEO Expert...  +  "SEO expert and web developer in Prishtina..."
```
